	"title": "COPD Assessment Test (CAT)",
	"description": "The COPD Assessment Test (CAT) is a patient-completed instrument that assesses and quantifies the impact of COPD symptoms on a patients' overall health.",
	"purpose": "A simple 8-item questionnaire used to assess the health status and symptom burden in individuals with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). It evaluates cough, phlegm, chest tightness, breathlessness, and activity limitations. Scores range from 0 to 40, with higher scores indicating more severe symptoms.",
